## Proof

**Claim.** For every $n \geq 1$, all $\ell^n$-torsion points of $E$ are rational over $K_S$:
$$E[\ell^n] \;=\; E[\ell^n](\overline{\mathbb{Q}}) \;\subseteq\; E(K_S).$$

Equivalently, the torsion field $\mathbb{Q}(E[\ell^n])$ is unramified outside $S$, hence $\mathbb{Q}(E[\ell^n]) \subseteq K_S$.

---

**Setup.** The absolute Galois group $G_{\mathbb{Q}} = \mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ acts on
$$E[\ell^n] \;=\; \{P \in E(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}) : \ell^n P = 0\} \;\cong\; (\mathbb{Z}/\ell^n\mathbb{Z})^2,$$
giving a mod-$\ell^n$ Galois representation
$$\rho_{\ell^n} : G_{\mathbb{Q}} \longrightarrow \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Z}/\ell^n\mathbb{Z}).$$
The fixed field of $\ker \rho_{\ell^n}$ is exactly $\mathbb{Q}(E[\ell^n])$, the field obtained by adjoining to $\mathbb{Q}$ the coordinates of all points in $E[\ell^n]$. Thus
$$\mathrm{Gal}\bigl(\mathbb{Q}(E[\ell^n])/\mathbb{Q}\bigr) \;\cong\; \mathrm{im}\,\rho_{\ell^n} \;\subseteq\; \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Z}/\ell^n\mathbb{Z}).$$

To prove $\mathbb{Q}(E[\ell^n]) \subseteq K_S$ it suffices to show $\mathbb{Q}(E[\ell^n])/\mathbb{Q}$ is unramified at every prime $p \notin S$.

---

**Key tool: Néron–Ogg–Shafarevich criterion.** For a prime $p \neq \ell$, the elliptic curve $E$ has good reduction at $p$ if and only if the $\ell$-adic Tate module
$$T_\ell(E) \;=\; \varprojlim_n E[\ell^n]$$
is unramified as a representation of the local decomposition group $G_{\mathbb{Q}_p} \subseteq G_{\mathbb{Q}}$.

(Equivalently: the inertia group $I_p \subseteq G_{\mathbb{Q}_p}$ acts trivially on $T_\ell(E)$.)

---

**Applying it.** Let $p \notin S$. By definition of $S$:
- $p \neq \ell$ (since $\ell \in S$), and
- $E$ has good reduction at $p$ (since all bad-reduction primes lie in $S$).

By Néron–Ogg–Shafarevich, $T_\ell(E)$ is unramified at $p$: the inertia group $I_p$ acts trivially on $T_\ell(E)$.

Now $T_\ell(E) = \varprojlim_n E[\ell^n]$ with transition maps being multiplication by $\ell$. For each $n$, the natural projection
$$T_\ell(E) \;\twoheadrightarrow\; T_\ell(E)/\ell^n T_\ell(E) \;\cong\; E[\ell^n]$$
is $G_{\mathbb{Q}}$-equivariant. Since $I_p$ acts trivially on $T_\ell(E)$, it acts trivially on every quotient $E[\ell^n]$. In other words, $I_p \subseteq \ker \rho_{\ell^n}$.

By Galois theory, $I_p \subseteq \ker \rho_{\ell^n}$ means precisely that the extension $\mathbb{Q}(E[\ell^n])/\mathbb{Q}$ is **unramified at $p$**.

---

**Conclusion.** We have shown: for every $p \notin S$, the extension $\mathbb{Q}(E[\ell^n])/\mathbb{Q}$ is unramified at $p$. Therefore $\mathbb{Q}(E[\ell^n])$ is unramified outside $S$, which is exactly the defining property of the maximal such extension:
$$\mathbb{Q}(E[\ell^n]) \;\subseteq\; K_S.$$

Consequently every $\ell^n$-torsion point of $E$ is defined over $K_S$:
$$E[\ell^n] \;\subseteq\; E(K_S) \qquad \text{for all } n \geq 1.$$

Passing to the direct limit, the full $\ell$-power torsion satisfies
$$E[\ell^\infty] \;=\; \bigcup_{n\geq 1} E[\ell^n] \;\subseteq\; E(K_S),$$
and the $\ell$-adic Tate module $T_\ell(E)$ is an unramified-outside-$S$ $G_{\mathbb{Q}}$-representation, with the associated $\ell$-adic representation
$$\rho_{\ell,\infty} : \mathrm{Gal}(K_S/\mathbb{Q}) \;\longrightarrow\; \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Z}_\ell)$$
factoring through $\mathrm{Gal}(K_S/\mathbb{Q})$.

**In words:** the field $K_S$ contains all $\ell$-power torsion of $E$; the $\ell$-adic Galois representation attached to $E$ factors through $\mathrm{Gal}(K_S/\mathbb{Q})$, i.e. it is unramified outside the set $S$ of bad primes together with $\ell$. This is precisely the content of the Néron–Ogg–Shafarevich criterion applied level-by-level to $E[\ell^n]$.

